;;; basw-top.scm -- STONE-WEIERSTRASS on a compact space, real and complex, from the tree's
;;; weierstrass-approximation (calculus 5.7).  Agent BA-SW, wave 2026-11-09.  Helper prefix: bst-.
;;; Destination: theorem-library/basw-top.scm.  Library: complex-analysis (weierstrass-approximation and
;;; cc-ps-shift are complex-analysis theorems), PROVIDED the four measure-library lemmas it cites
;;; (big-union-of-empty-family, big-union-of-singleton-family, big-union-of-union-family in
;;; measure-ch1-algebras; abs-mul-le-unit in complex-measure-laws) move to core / analysis; otherwise
;;; operator-algebras (imports complex-analysis and measure).
;;; Vocabulary: structure-library/basw-vocab.scm (RCONT, IS-RCONT-SUBALGEBRA, IS-POINT-SEPARATING,
;;; RCONT-CLOSURE, IS-CCONT-STAR-SUBALGEBRA).
;;;
;;;   continuity read pointwise: bsw-cont-local, bsw-local-cont, bsw-rcont-*, bsw-cc-elim,
;;;     bsw-rcont-of-cc, bsw-rcont-re, bsw-rcont-im
;;;   bsw-compact-induction  a class of subsets of PTS t containing EMPTY-SET, closed under binary
;;;     unions, and containing an open neighbourhood of every point, contains PTS t (t compact)
;;;   bsw-rcont-bounded      a continuous real function on a compact space is bounded
;;;   the closure RCONT-CLOSURE(t, aa) is closed, contains aa, and is closed under |.|
;;;     (bsw-ucl-abs, through Weierstrass on [-(M+1), M+1]), combinations, max and min
;;;   bsw-sw-step1/2         the two compactness inductions of the lattice proof
;;;   bsw-stone-weierstrass-real(-dense), bsw-stone-weierstrass-complex
;;;
;;; No Hausdorff hypothesis: separation of points by aa is all the proof uses.
